# Uncorrelated subqueries as values in a query block that aggregates (ADR 0041's SQ2, its second PR): a select item
# or an ORDER BY item over GROUP BY keys and aggregates, in grouped and global blocks, joined after the aggregation; a
# GROUP BY key and an aggregate's argument, joined per row, a key matched by the same expression, its alias or its
# position; HAVING over the alias of a value item; and such blocks inside derived tables, CTEs, compounds, IN, scalar
# and EXISTS subqueries. Every value is computed before any row is read, so its row error fails both engines.

# ---- values over aggregates and keys ----

# A value as a select item of a grouped block: alone, the same on every group; over COUNT, SUM (HUGEINT), AVG and
# MIN/MAX; two values in one item; in a function, COALESCE and a cast; over a join's groups.

